{"c":[{"id":"d174639a9c85f705","sum":"J1: Jev confidence is (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n); a daily spend cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP $0.50) throws JevCapError; the replay cache takes fixture text only; TypeSafe's MCA s2.3(b) forbids distilling Jev output.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"987e4b1534648136","sum":"J1: Jev confidence is (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n) over n options (not the top-two margin judge.ts says; equal only for n=2); makeJevClient holds a per-day spend cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP, default $0.50) and throws JevCapError; vitest uses a temp spend dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T065440Z-6320f5713756d4a4","text":"J1: TypeSafe documents Jev's Choice confidence as (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n) over n options (docs.typesafe.ai/confidence), not the top-two margin routing/judge.ts describes; the two agree only for two options. engines/decide/confidence.ts computes other engines' confidence this way.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T065544Z-2b923d2a58b8f2cf","text":"J1: makeJevClient holds every request against a per-day spend file (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP, default $0.50; CARET_JEV_SPEND_DIR) and throws JevCapError (kind cap) past it; vitest.config.ts points the spend dir at a temp dir.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0d659675b89b1bba","sum":"J1: the replay cache and --log-requests take only fixture text (harness lists fixture window ids; the helper refuses the cache); TypeSafe's MCA s2.3(b) forbids distilling Jev output: train local models on Caret's answer keys or a permissive teacher.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T065553Z-29f2d5c421092ef7","text":"J1: the replay cache (engines/decide/cache.ts) and --log-requests take only fixture text: a harness lists its fixture window ids and says if its memory and plan text (window id 'plan') are fixtures; charged windows are checked too. The helper refuses CARET_JEV_CACHE.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T065553Z-310f47ee41817c11","text":"J1: TypeSafe's Master Customer Agreement s2.3(b) (2026-09-23) forbids using Jev's Output for distillation or to train an imitating model; train a local model on Caret's answer keys or a permissive teacher instead.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1e39825f89d0ff0d","sum":"H12-H13: inject a test pageField via the host debug socket (the bundled helper gets allowlisted env only); page inline offers are OfferSource.page and Tab sends pageInsert; a note window needs its own app in helper tests; launchd's argv0 is relative.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"379ec0af76ae5f62","sum":"H13: the bundled helper gets only allowlisted env (ServiceLauncher), so inject a test pageField via the host debug socket; page inline offers are OfferSource.page (native ghost clears skip them), insertsText false, and Tab sends pageInsert.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T080508Z-2110f7480275cbcf","text":"H13: the bundled helper gets only allowlisted env (ServiceLauncher: HOME, USER, LANG, TYPESAFE_API_KEY, CARET_ENV_FILE...), so a helper-side test switch never reaches it from Caret.app; inject a pageField through the host debug socket instead.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T080508Z-bc4a09143ef1ff5b","text":"H13: page inline offers use OfferSource.page (never .engine), so HostCoordinator's ghost clears on AX focus changes leave them alone; Claim.insertsText is false for a page ghost and PageInlineMachine sends pageInsert.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"940d166167db3d8d","sum":"H12-H13: launchd starts the agent with relative argv0 'Contents/MacOS/Caret' (use launchctl print's pid or lsof); in helper tests a non-page window with the browser's pid is passed over as Chrome's toolbar, so give a note window its own app.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T080508Z-ed6af011d8df3dcf","text":"H13: in helper tests, a non-page window sharing the page's browser pid is passed over as Chrome's toolbar (H10 ScreenModel.windowBefore); give a note window its own app (NOTES_APP) or TabSource reads the wrong tab.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T082217Z-6e9f887494c1affe","text":"H12: launchd starts the SMAppService agent as relative argv0 'Contents/MacOS/Caret', so pgrep/ps matching on /Applications/Caret.app misses the host; use launchctl print's pid or lsof txt. A fresh VM guest makes no helper Jev request (no transfers), fill or first look.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
